<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Alexander the Great</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">r. 336–323 BCE</span> · Also known as Alexander III of Macedon</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Alexander the Great, Alexander III of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-macedon">Macedon</a>, was king of Macedon from 336 to 323 BCE. He conquered the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/achaemenid-empire">Achaemenid Empire</a> and led his army as far as the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/indus">Indus</a> valley, creating the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/macedonian-empire">Macedonian Empire</a>. After his death his generals divided his conquests, founding successor states such as the Ptolemaic and Seleucid empires, and his campaigns spread Greek culture across the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/near-east">Near East</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/alexander-the-great.jpg" alt="Alexander the Great" width="315" height="420" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown authorUnknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Alexander_Mosaic_detail_of_Alexander_the_Great_(3x4_cropped).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
